3:T113f,<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Trigger finger, or stenosing tenosynovitis, is a condition that causes pain, stiffness, and a sensation of locking or catching when you bend and straighten your finger. It's a common ailment affecting individuals across various age groups, including many patients in Hyderabad. Understanding the difference between trigger finger surgery and injection treatment is crucial for making an informed decision about your health. With the expertise of Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, patients have access to the latest treatment options tailored to their needs.</p>

<h2>Understanding Trigger Finger</h2>
<p>Trigger finger occurs when inflammation narrows the space within the sheath that surrounds the tendon in the affected finger. This can cause discomfort and difficulties in performing everyday tasks. In Hyderabad, many patients seek orthopedic care to alleviate these symptoms and restore finger function. Two primary treatments—surgery and injections—are often considered. An understanding of each option can help patients choose the best treatment in consultation with an experienced orthopedic specialist like Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy.</p>

<h2>Symptoms and Diagnosis</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pain and a clicking sensation when moving the finger</li>
<li>Stiffness in the finger, especially in the morning</li>
<li>Finger locked in a bent position, which may suddenly pop straight</li>
<li>Swelling or a tender lump at the base of the finger</li>
</ul>
<p>Dr. Reddy begins by assessing the symptoms and performing a physical examination to diagnose trigger finger accurately. Patients at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad can expect a thorough evaluation to determine the severity of the condition and the most suitable course of treatment.</p>

<h2>Treatment Options</h2>
<p>The two main treatment options for trigger finger are surgical intervention and steroid injections. Choosing the right option depends on the severity of your symptoms and your overall health.</p>
<p><strong>1. Surgical Treatment:</strong> Trigger finger surgery involves making a small incision at the base of the finger to release the tightened sheath. This procedure is typically performed on an outpatient basis and offers a permanent solution to those who do not respond to more conservative measures.</p>
<p><strong>2. Injection Therapy:</strong> Corticosteroid injections can reduce inflammation and swelling, allowing the tendon to glide more freely. This non-invasive option can be an effective treatment for mild to moderate cases of trigger finger, providing relief for many patients.</p>
<p>Working with an expert like Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy at Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, ensures access to the most advanced approaches and a personalized treatment plan that prioritizes patient safety and optimal outcomes.</p>

<h2>Why Choose Dr. Harsha at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</h2>
<p>Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy is renowned for his expertise in orthopedic care and his commitment to patient-centered treatment. At Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad, patients benefit from state-of-the-art facilities and compassionate care. Dr. Reddy offers a comprehensive evaluation to determine whether trigger finger surgery or injection therapy is suitable for your condition. His patient-centric approach ensures that you receive a treatment plan tailored to your specific needs.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How long is the recovery time after trigger finger surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: Recovery typically takes a few weeks, during which time you'll need to perform specific exercises to restore full movement and strength.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Are injections painful?</strong></p>
<p>A: Corticosteroid injections may cause mild discomfort, but the procedure is short, and most patients find it manageable.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Can trigger finger recur after treatment?</strong></p>
<p>A: While surgery offers a more permanent solution, there is a chance of recurrence. Regular follow-ups with Dr. Reddy can help monitor your condition.</p>

<h2>Book Your Appointment</h2>
<p>Call Dr. Harsha at <strong>+91 99599 64567</strong> or visit Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Nanakramguda, Hyderabad. Take the first step towards recovery and regain your finger's full function with expert care.</p>5:["slug","trigger-finger-surgery-vs-injection-treatment-latest-treatment-options-hyderabad","d"]
